  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Human Capital Empowerment in Myanmar (HCEM)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mahidol-Norway Capacity Building Initiative for Myanmar (CBIM Phase 3) is expected to provide at least 16 Bachelor&#x2019;s and 28 Master&#x2019;s scholarships as well as 2 capacity building projects for Myanmar citizens. The targeted areas include population studies, public health and other healthcare studies, environment and resource studies, physical therapy, engineering, information technology and basic science. For Bachelor&#x2019;s degree programmes, the focus is on engineering, information technology and basic science as these areas are believed to assist the country in basic infrastructure development as seen needed for the future advancement. For Master&#x2019;s degree programmes, emphasis is put on areas in public health and other healthcare programmes, environment, and more advanced engineering and so on, as to help some sectors in Myanmar to prepare their human resources for the future economic and social needs.</narrative>
  </description>
